nse as a free function or constructor since it's building a `BbrPerAckState` from other data rather than mutating an existing `BbrState`. Setting the delivery rate based on available bandwidth estimates or falling back to a default, then populating the rest of the rate sample structure with acknowledgment metrics like newly acked bytes, loss information, and congestion state flags.\n\nNow I'm realizing there's a type mismatch in the Rust port—the RTT values are `Duration` objects rather than raw microseconds, so I need to extract the underlying tick count when calculating the delivery rate.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1294,"cache_read_input_tokens":58253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1294},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5be31241-b87d-4d1b-a6ec-ddeef1119c85","uuid":"b4305972-ebaa-4b44-af76-3ecd4e413e9d"}
